":"Borrowed from German Zylinder, from Latin cylindrus, from Ancient Greek κύλινδρος (kúlindros). Compare Russian цили́ндр (cilíndr), Belarusian цылі́ндр (cylíndr).","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"циркуль","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"pair of compasses, compass (device used to draw circular arcs and transfer length measurements)","termine_origine":"Zirkel","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Zirkel","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"circinus","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Zirkel, from Latin circulus.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"циркуляр","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"circulaire (written directive to subordinates)","termine_origine":"Zirkular","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Zirkular","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"circulāris","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Zirkular (“circular (notice for mass distribution)”), from Latin circulāris.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"циркуляція","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"circulation (the act of moving in a circle, or in a course which brings the moving body to the place where its motion b…","termine_origine":"Zirkulation","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Zirkulation","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"circulātiō","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["mare"],"via":"","testo":"Probably borrowed from German Zirkulation (along with циркулюва́ти (cyrkuljuváty) from zirkulieren), from Latin circulātiō. Compare Russian циркуля́ция (cirkuljácija), Belarusian цыркуля́цыя (cyrkuljácyja), Polish cyrkulacja.","livello2_varieta":"la"},{"parola":"ш